{"id": "De3bxWFRIR6", "title": "Video by therishikatha", "description": "That cute golden deer was a DEMON 🦌 And Ram had beaten him before. Plus: there's NO Lakshman Rekha in Valmiki's Ramayan | Ramayan Part 6 of 12\n\n👑 Ravana heard what Ram did, and wanted revenge. He went to the demon Maricha for help, and Maricha shook with fear. (Aranya Kanda 31–39)\n🌊 Years ago, a boy named Ram had shot him into the ocean, a hundred yojanas away! (Bala Kanda 30)\n🗡️ \"Help me,\" said Ravana, \"or die by my sword.\" Maricha thought: better to die by Ram's arrow. (Aranya 40–41)\n✨ He turned into a golden deer: silver spots, jewelled antlers. Sita said: \"Catch it for me, please!\" Lakshman warned: \"No deer looks like that. It's Maricha!\" (Aranya 42–43)\n🏹 Ram told Lakshman: guard Sita. He chased the deer, but it kept vanishing and appearing. At last his arrow struck, and the dying demon cried in Ram's own voice: \"Ha Sita! Ha Lakshman!\" (Aranya 44)\n💔 Sita begged Lakshman to go. He said no. Then her words were so harsh, he had to go. (Aranya 45)\n❌ And no, he drew no line. There is NO Lakshman Rekha in Valmiki's Ramayan: it comes from later tellings.\n🚪 Sita was alone. Then a holy man came to the door…\n\n➡️ Part 7: the holy man was RAVANA. Follow @therishikatha so you don't miss it!\n\n📚 Rishi Katha picture books tell our gods' stories for kids, in simple words and bright pictures. Insta Family Sale on Books 1–3, till 25 Oct → rishikatha.com (link in bio)\n\n💬 Comment JAI SHRI RAM if you're watching the whole series 🙏\n🔖 Save this, and share it with someone who still believes in the Lakshman Rekha 😄\n\n#ramayan #ramayana #goldendeer #maricha #lakshmanrekha #sita #valmikiramayana #jaishriram #sanatandharma #hindumythology #indianmythology #ramayanseries #kidsbooks #rishikatha", "channel": "therishikatha", "uploader_id": "22569163881", "uploader": "Rishi Katha", "timestamp": 1792821571, "like_count": 838, "comment_count": 31, "http_headers": {"Referer": "https://www.instagram.